{title: 452 - What Heavenly Music}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #452 • HEAVENLY MUSIC • 11.11.12.11}
{lyricist: James White}
{composer: From Hymns and Tunes}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 452}
{meta: tune HEAVENLY MUSIC}
{meta: meter 11.11.12.11}
{meta: category Early Advent - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]What heavenly music [C]steals over the sea!
[Gm/Bb]Entrancing [F]the senses like sweet melody!
[C]Tis the voice of [Dm]the [Bb]angels [C7]born [C]soft on the air
[F]For me they [Am]are singing; [Gm]their welcome [Dm]Ihear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]On the banks of old Jordan, [C]here gazing I [Dm]stand,
[Gm/Bb]And earnestly [F]longing, I stretch forth my hand;
[C]Send a convoy [Dm]of [Bb]angels, [C7]dear [C]Jesus, I pray!
[F]Let me join [Am]that sweet music; [Gm]come, [Dm]take me away.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Though dark are the waters [C]and rough is the wave,
[Gm/Bb]If Jesus [F]permit, the wild surges I'll brave;
[C]For that heavenly [Bb]music [C7]hath [C]ravished me so,
[F]I must join [Am]in that chorus! [Gm]I'll [Dm]go! let me [F/C]go!
{end_of_verse}
